    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RAG Workflow for Knowledge Base - Delete\n\n## Purpose\nRemoves knowledge-base files from the Pinecone vector store (and downstream PageIndex) so the chatbot stops retrieving deleted or stale content. Supports both an autonomous Drive-sweep (detects files that disappeared from the Knowledge_Base folder) and a programmatic sub-workflow path used by other automations.\n\n## How it works\n- Scheduled-sweep path (every 2 minutes): lists everything in the Knowledge_Base Drive folder, compares against the Rag_File_Tracker sheet, and categorizes tracked files as `toDelete` (missing on second check), `toMarkMissing` (missing once  give it a grace period), or `toMarkActive` (reappeared after being missing). For toDelete files it removes vectors from Pinecone, marks the tracker row deleted, then forwards to the PageIndex delete sub-workflow\n- Sub-workflow path: receives `fileId` + `fileName` from a caller, deletes the file from Drive, removes its Pinecone vectors, marks the tracker row deleted, then forwards to the PageIndex delete sub-workflow\n- Both paths converge on the same PageIndex cleanup so the two stores stay aligned\n\n## Triggered by\n- Schedule trigger  every 2 minutes (autonomous Drive sweep)\n- Execute Workflow trigger with `fileId` + `fileName` (sub-workflow path)\n\n## Calls (sub-workflows)\n- PageIndex Workflow for Knowledge Base - Delete  called from BOTH the scheduled-sweep path (after the tracker row is marked deleted) and the explicit sub-workflow path, so PageIndex stays consistent with Pinecone regardless of how the deletion was triggered.\n\n## Called by\n- Human Cases RAG Updater\n\n## Reads/writes\n- Reads (and on the sub-workflow path, deletes from) Google Drive `Knowledge_Base` folder\n- Deletes vectors from Pinecone index `company-files`\n- Reads and upserts Google Sheets `Customer_Support_Data`  `Rag_File_Tracker`",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview-doc",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1200,
        -400
      ]
    }
  ],
